    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe refactor is a clean, coherent consolidation that follows the codebase's established conventions:\n\n- **Logic is in the right unit.** The check-digit (Luhn) computation moved out of `OwnerMapper` (where it was a DTO-derived field) into `AssignOwnerMemberId`, which is now the single assembly point for the composite id. That matches the spec's intent (CHK is a segment of the id, computed at assignment, no longer a standalone derived field). `sha256Hex8` moved with it from the deleted `AssignOwnerCustomerCode`. No logic is duplicated as a result.\n\n- **The mapper got simpler, not heavier.** Two derived methods (`checkDigit`, `membershipNumber`) were removed outright rather than rewired, and `locality` now delegates to `OwnerRegion.regionFromMemberId`. Nothing became a catch-all.\n\n- **Each source-of-truth stays focused.** `OwnerRegion` still owns the region value, `OwnerFiscalYear` still owns the FY value, and `AssignOwnerMemberId` assembles the segments \u2014 a consistent \"value from the owner class, rendering in the id builder\" split. The FY two-digit (`%02d` of `% 100`) rendering living in the builder rather than `OwnerFiscalYear` is defensible, since that's an id-formatting concern, not the FY value itself.\n\n- **The one cross-unit coupling is handled sensibly.** `regionFromMemberId` must know the fixed `<FY><HASH8><CHK>` suffix length (11) because the id is delimiter-less. Putting that as a documented local constant in `OwnerRegion` (rather than referencing `AssignOwnerMemberId`) is the right call \u2014 `AssignOwnerMemberId` already depends on `OwnerRegion`, so the alternative would introduce a cycle. The comment spelling out `2 + 8 + 1` keeps it legible.\n\n- **Doc/comment coherence is thorough.** The forward-looking \"when it is later unified into memberId\u2026\" comments in `OwnerCreatedEvent` and `AuditOwnerCreated#primaryIdentifier` were resolved rather than left stale, and the OpenAPI/schema/javadoc references were all updated consistently. The `primaryIdentifier` seam is reasonable to retain as the single point naming the event's identifier.\n\nA maintainer of this project would find the result natural.",
